    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find $f(x)$, and then find $f(2)$, given that:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f'(x)=1+\\dfrac{2}{x}$ and $f(1)=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(x)=x+2\\ln|x|$; $f(2)=2+2\\ln 2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=x+2\\ln|x|+C\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $f(1)=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1+2\\ln 1+C&=1\\\\1+0+C&=1\\\\C&=0\\\\f(x)&=x+2\\ln|x|\\\\f(2)&=2+2\\ln 2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f'(x)=3+\\dfrac{5}{2x-1}$ and $f(1)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(x)=3x+\\dfrac52\\ln|2x-1|-3$; $f(2)=3+\\dfrac52\\ln 3$.",
          "worked": {
